WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.435 --> 00:00:09.197
There once was a woodcutter who lived in Germany.

2
00:00:09.797 --> 00:00:13.099
He had two children named Hansel and Gretel.

3
00:00:13.739 --> 00:00:16.160
They lived together in a house in the forest.

4
00:00:17.221 --> 00:00:22.044
During the winter the woodcutter would go deep into the forest to cut firewood.

5
00:00:22.664 --> 00:00:28.387
When he came home, he and Hansel and Gretel would take the firewood to town to sell it

6
00:00:28.747 --> 00:00:29.608
and buy food.

7
00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:34.935
"Good-bye, children," said the woodcutter.

8
00:00:34.955 --> 00:00:37.497
"I am going to cut firewood.

9
00:00:38.217 --> 00:00:40.239
I will come home tonight for dinner."

10
00:00:40.259 --> 00:00:44.382
"Good-bye, Father," said Hansel and Gretel.

11
00:00:45.203 --> 00:00:47.485
And they waved as their father walked away.

12
00:00:51.068 --> 00:00:54.030
Dinnertime came and the woodcutter did not come home.

13
00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:56.032
"Where is Father?"

14
00:00:56.753 --> 00:00:57.533
asked Gretel.

15
00:00:58.394 --> 00:01:04.189
"I don't know," said Hansel, "but we won't eat dinner until he comes home."

16
00:01:05.109 --> 00:01:07.350
They waited and waited and waited.

17
00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:10.130
They waited so long they fell asleep.

18
00:01:13.972 --> 00:01:16.952
When they woke up, the sun was shining through the windows.

19
00:01:16.972 --> 00:01:18.653
"Oh no!"

20
00:01:19.293 --> 00:01:19.973
said Hansel.

21
00:01:19.993 --> 00:01:22.314
"Father did not come home!

22
00:01:22.974 --> 00:01:24.394
Something must have happened.

23
00:01:24.935 --> 00:01:26.415
We must go look for him."

24
00:01:27.155 --> 00:01:29.996
They packed some bread to eat and walked into the woods.

25
00:01:31.568 --> 00:01:32.568
"Wait, Hansel.

26
00:01:33.149 --> 00:01:35.089
How will we find our way home?"

27
00:01:35.549 --> 00:01:36.189
asked Gretel.

28
00:01:36.209 --> 00:01:38.310
"Uhh Oh!

29
00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:44.292
I will leave bread crumbs in the path to show us how to get home," said Hansel.

30
00:01:44.912 --> 00:01:47.032
"Good idea," Gretel said.

31
00:01:47.652 --> 00:01:50.733
They walked for hours and hours and hours.

32
00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:56.915
Because they had used their bread to show the way home, they had nothing to eat.

33
00:01:56.935 --> 00:02:00.256
"I am getting hungry," said Hansel.

34
00:02:01.444 --> 00:02:05.688
"Yes, and I am getting cold too," said Gretel.

35
00:02:05.708 --> 00:02:07.450
"It is getting late.

36
00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:09.492
Maybe we should go home.

37
00:02:10.212 --> 00:02:12.454
Maybe Father is waiting there for us."

38
00:02:12.474 --> 00:02:15.237
"Yes, maybe he is.

39
00:02:15.697 --> 00:02:18.180
Let's go home," Hansel agreed.

40
00:02:19.381 --> 00:02:23.945
But, when they turned around to go home, they did not know which way to go.

41
00:02:23.965 --> 00:02:26.087
"Oh no!"

42
00:02:26.587 --> 00:02:27.188
said Gretel.

43
00:02:28.168 --> 00:02:29.788
"Our bread crumbs are gone!

44
00:02:29.809 --> 00:02:32.129
How will we find our way home?"

45
00:02:32.149 --> 00:02:36.930
"The birds must have eaten all our crumbs," said Hansel.

46
00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:41.712
"Maybe home is this way," said Gretel.

47
00:02:42.292 --> 00:02:44.693
They walked and walked and walked.

48
00:02:46.653 --> 00:02:49.194
Finally they saw smoke coming from a chimney.

49
00:02:49.214 --> 00:02:51.094
"It must be Father!"

50
00:02:51.654 --> 00:02:54.235
the children cried, and they ran to the house.

51
00:02:55.035 --> 00:02:57.056
But the smoke was not their father's.

52
00:02:57.756 --> 00:02:59.157
It was a magical house.

53
00:02:59.878 --> 00:03:05.261
Its walls were made of cookies, its roof was made of peppermint, and the doors were made of

54
00:03:05.342 --> 00:03:07.803
chocolate. "Wow!"

55
00:03:08.344 --> 00:03:09.625
said Hansel and Gretel.

56
00:03:11.546 --> 00:03:13.267
And they began to eat the house.

57
00:03:15.469 --> 00:03:20.252
What Hansel and Gretel didn't know was that inside the house lived a witch.

58
00:03:21.053 --> 00:03:25.496
While Hansel was busy eating, the witch opened the door and grabbed him.

59
00:03:26.732 --> 00:03:28.553
"Who is eating my house?"

60
00:03:29.494 --> 00:03:30.274
asked the witch.

61
00:03:30.835 --> 00:03:32.136
She was very angry.

62
00:03:32.156 --> 00:03:35.998
"I didn't know it was your house," said Hansel.

63
00:03:36.018 --> 00:03:40.201
"We're very sorry," said Gretel.

64
00:03:40.221 --> 00:03:42.343
"Please let him go."

65
00:03:42.363 --> 00:03:48.347
"No. He has eaten my house, and now I will eat him."

66
00:03:49.067 --> 00:03:52.310
The witch dragged Hansel into a cage and locked him inside.

67
00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:57.045
"And you will be my servant," she said to Gretel.

68
00:03:57.725 --> 00:03:59.887
Then the witch laughed a terrible laugh.

69
00:04:01.788 --> 00:04:07.012
The witch fed Hansel lots and lots of food to make him fat, so that he would be

70
00:04:07.052 --> 00:04:08.152
a delicious dinner.

71
00:04:08.873 --> 00:04:14.537
But the witch had very old eyes that made everything seem blurry, and she could not see if

72
00:04:14.597 --> 00:04:15.638
Hansel was fat.

73
00:04:17.018 --> 00:04:23.523
So every day she would say to Hansel, "Put out your finger," and she would feel it to

74
00:04:23.583 --> 00:04:24.804
see if he was fat enough.

75
00:04:26.764 --> 00:04:27.845
Hansel was smart.

76
00:04:28.305 --> 00:04:30.848
He did not put out his finger when the witch asked.

77
00:04:31.368 --> 00:04:34.491
He saved a bone from his dinner and put that out instead.

78
00:04:35.231 --> 00:04:39.054
The witch would feel the bone and say, "Not fat enough.

79
00:04:39.555 --> 00:04:41.736
Maybe I will eat him tomorrow."

80
00:04:41.757 --> 00:04:45.420
Gretel cried every day.

81
00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.842
She didn't want her brother to be eaten.

82
00:04:48.722 --> 00:04:50.063
Finally the day came.

83
00:04:50.083 --> 00:04:55.408
"Put out your finger," the witch asked.

84
00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:57.341
Hansel put out the bone.

85
00:04:58.042 --> 00:04:59.483
"Still not fat enough.

86
00:05:00.104 --> 00:05:02.466
Well, I am not going to wait.

87
00:05:03.086 --> 00:05:04.467
I will eat you tonight!"

88
00:05:05.308 --> 00:05:07.950
When Gretel heard this, she cried even harder.

89
00:05:08.711 --> 00:05:10.712
"Stop crying, silly girl!"

90
00:05:11.433 --> 00:05:12.234
the witch said.

91
00:05:12.254 --> 00:05:17.438
"Crawl inside that oven and make a fire to cook dinner."

92
00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:20.721
Gretel was smart too.

93
00:05:21.201 --> 00:05:26.414
She knew the witch was trying to trick her, so she said, "I don't know how to climb

94
00:05:26.494 --> 00:05:27.414
into an oven."

95
00:05:27.895 --> 00:05:30.417
"Stupid girl," the witch said.

96
00:05:30.437 --> 00:05:33.880
"I will show you, and then you will do it."

97
00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:36.862
The witch climbed inside the oven to show Gretel.

98
00:05:37.363 --> 00:05:41.966
But just as she was inside, Gretel shut the oven door and locked it.

99
00:05:44.428 --> 00:05:45.469
"Let me out!"

100
00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:46.890
cried the witch.

101
00:05:46.911 --> 00:05:49.393
"I promise not to eat you!

102
00:05:49.413 --> 00:05:51.214
I'm very sorry.

103
00:05:51.614 --> 00:05:53.256
Please let me out!"

104
00:05:53.932 --> 00:05:55.973
But the children did not listen to her.

105
00:05:56.633 --> 00:06:01.594
Gretel freed Hansel from his cage and they ran away from the witch's candy house as fast as

106
00:06:01.634 --> 00:06:02.114
they could.

107
00:06:05.395 --> 00:06:07.556
They ran and ran and ran.

108
00:06:08.316 --> 00:06:10.576
They saw another chimney with smoke coming out.

109
00:06:11.957 --> 00:06:14.838
"We must be careful, Hansel," said Gretel.

110
00:06:15.458 --> 00:06:17.338
She did not want to meet another witch.

111
00:06:18.018 --> 00:06:19.859
They walked quietly up to the house.

112
00:06:20.799 --> 00:06:23.580
Just then the door opened and the woodcutter walked out.

113
00:06:24.876 --> 00:06:26.397
"Father! Father!

114
00:06:26.417 --> 00:06:28.698
Father!" they cried.

115
00:06:29.318 --> 00:06:31.459
And they ran to him with their arms open.

116
00:06:32.019 --> 00:06:33.780
He gave them a big hug.

117
00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:35.720
"Hansel! Gretel!

118
00:06:36.061 --> 00:06:37.141
Where have you been!

119
00:06:37.161 --> 00:06:39.262
I was so worried about you!"

120
00:06:39.282 --> 00:06:43.203
"We went looking for you, Father," said Gretel.

121
00:06:43.223 --> 00:06:51.247
"Yes, you didn't come home so we went to find you," said Hansel.

122
00:06:51.267 --> 00:06:54.508
"Ah, I'm sorry, children.

123
00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:58.743
I broke my leg and came home the next day.

124
00:06:59.663 --> 00:07:00.704
But you were gone.

125
00:07:01.345 --> 00:07:03.766
You must never go into the forest alone.

126
00:07:04.287 --> 00:07:06.548
There are dangerous things in the forest."

127
00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:09.250
"Yes, Father.

128
00:07:09.591 --> 00:07:13.333
There are dangerous things in the forest," they said.

129
00:07:13.974 --> 00:07:16.896
Hansel and Gretel went inside the house with their father.

130
00:07:17.376 --> 00:07:19.478
They decided to tell him about the witch.

131
00:07:20.118 --> 00:07:22.260
But first they would eat dinner.
